

1. What is MongoDB?

MongoDB is a NoSQL, document-oriented database used to store application data.

Unlike SQL databases, MongoDB stores data in the form of documents instead of rows and tables.

Example:

{
  "name": "Gaurav",
  "email": "gaurav@gmail.com",
  "age": 21
}

MongoDB stores these documents inside collections.

MongoDB Structure

Database
   ↓
Collection
   ↓
Document
   ↓
Fields

Example:

myDatabase
   ↓
users
   ↓
{
   name: "Gaurav",
   email: "gaurav@gmail.com"
}

